      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/nodes/clusters/nodes-cluster-limit-ranges#nodes-cluster-limit-ranges-about_nodes-cluster-limit-ranges">About limit ranges</a></li>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/scalability_and_performance/recommended-performance-scale-practices/recommended-control-plane-practices#recommended-scale-practices_recommended-control-plane-practices">Recommended control plane practices</a></li>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/storage/understanding-ephemeral-storage#storage-ephemeral-storage-overview_understanding-ephemeral-storage">Understanding ephemeral storage</a></li>
      </ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="admin-limit-operations_using-quotas-and-limit-ranges" class="group scroll-mt-20">Limit range operations<a href="#admin-limit-operations_using-quotas-and-limit-ranges" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can create, view, and delete limit ranges in a project.</p>
      <p>You can view any limit ranges that are defined in a project by navigating in the web console to the <strong>Quota</strong> page for the project. You can also use the CLI to view limit range details.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      To create the object, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <limit_range_file> -n <project>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To view the list of limit range objects that exist in a project, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get limits -n demoproject"} lang="terminal" title="Example command with a project called demoproject" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME              AGE\nresource-limits   6d"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To describe a limit range, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc describe limits resource-limits -n demoproject"} lang="terminal" title="Example command with a limit range called resource-limits" />
      <CodeBlock code={"Name:                           resource-limits\nNamespace:                      demoproject\nType                            Resource                Min     Max     Default Request Default Limit   Max Limit/Request Ratio\n----                            --------                ---     ---     --------------- -------------   -----------------------\nPod                             cpu                     200m    2       -               -               -\nPod                             memory                  6Mi     1Gi     -               -               -\nContainer                       cpu                     100m    2       200m            300m            10\nContainer                       memory                  4Mi     1Gi     100Mi           200Mi           -\nopenshift.io/Image              storage                 -       1Gi     -               -               -\nopenshift.io/ImageStream        openshift.io/image      -       12      -               -               -\nopenshift.io/ImageStream        openshift.io/image-tags -       10      -               -               -"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      To delete a limit range, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete limits <limit_name>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
